Add attendee self-registration, for logged-in users with any authentication plugin and, when allowed, anonymous visitors who confirm their email address. Each event opts in with an Attendees database, which has a registration prefix, a confirmation policy, a registration deadline that ends registration even while the database is open, and a created, open and closed workflow. The database is a page with blocks that starts with the registration block, so it is the registration page of the event; once opened, it is public and shows in the navigation, also after it is closed, but only organizers can list its registrations. An event can offer tickets by adding Ticket items to its Attendees database, each with an optional period of availability: registrants then choose one, and each Attendee holds it. Registrations are named with codes such as `PYC26-7KQ3M9XD`, move through the pending, registered, attended and cancelled states, and are handled by the new `@registration` endpoint on the event root and `@attendees` endpoint on the Attendees database. @ericof
